workflow bug_hunter
  goal: "Given a bug report, reproduce it with a failing test, fix the root cause, run the GIVEN oracle (that test plus the tests that already passed), and deliver — READY only when the oracle is green, otherwise an honest DRAFT."
  # category: Fix a bug
  start: Start
  exit: Exit

  defaults
    max_retries: 2
    fidelity: summary:high
    max_restarts: 5

  tool Start
    label: Start
    timeout: 10s
    command:
      echo "start"

  tool Exit
    label: Exit
    timeout: 10s
    command:
      echo "exit"

  tool EnsureEnv
    label: "Bootstrap Environment"
    marker_grep: '^(env-ready|env-failed)$'
    timeout: 8m
    command:
      #!/bin/sh
      # GENERAL, seed-driven environment bootstrap. If the seed ships an executable
      # bootstrap hook, run it ONCE up front so a pinned, project-local toolchain
      # (e.g. ./.venv for Python, node_modules for JS, a toolchain pin for Go/Rust)
      # exists before any agent or gate runs a test. The pipeline stays language- and
      # repo-agnostic: it knows nothing about the project; it only runs the seed's hook
      # if one is present. No hook -> clean no-op (the common case; most repos ship none).
      #
      # FAIL LOUD (#846): a hook that is PRESENT and EXITS NON-ZERO means the pinned
      # dependency/toolchain setup did not complete. Swallowing that (the old
      # `|| echo continuing`) let the agent improvise its own deps and burn the whole run
      # on a doomed env (E1: 38m/$2.13 building numpy from source because the pinned wheel
      # was missing). So we RECORD the outcome to .tracker/env-bootstrap.status (+ .log,
      # read by the capability preflight) and emit a DISTINCT marker: `env-ready` on
      # success/no-hook (advance), `env-failed` on a failed hook (routes OUT of the work
      # loop to an honest DRAFT). The marker_grep regex lifts the marker into the typed
      # ctx.tool_marker routing channel (last matching line wins), so a stray diagnostic on
      # stdout can no longer flip routing; hook output still goes to the log/stderr.
      #
      # DENY BY DEFAULT: this node also STAMPS the delivery note as an unverified DRAFT
      # before any work starts. Nothing in this branch is backed by a passing test until
      # the Verify oracle overwrites this note with evidence. Every later node may only
      # replace it with its OWN result; the delivery agent may never author a verdict.
      set -u
      mkdir -p .tracker
      status_file=.tracker/env-bootstrap.status
      log_file=.tracker/env-bootstrap.log
      : > "$log_file"
      cat > .tracker/DELIVERY-NOTE.md <<'NOTE'
      DRAFT — NOT VERIFIED

      The verification gate has not run, so nothing here is backed by a passing test.
      Treat every claim in this branch as unverified until a human runs the tests.
      NOTE
      found=''
      for hook in bughunt-setup.sh .bughunt/setup.sh scripts/bughunt-setup.sh; do
        if [ -f "$hook" ]; then found="$hook"; break; fi
      done
      if [ -z "$found" ]; then
        printf 'status=ok\nhook=\nexit=0\n' > "$status_file"
        printf 'env-ready'
        exit 0
      fi
      echo "[EnsureEnv] running seed bootstrap hook: $found" >&2
      sh "$found" > "$log_file" 2>&1
      rc=$?
      cat "$log_file" >&2
      if [ "$rc" -eq 0 ]; then
        printf 'status=ok\nhook=%s\nexit=0\n' "$found" > "$status_file"
        printf 'env-ready'
      else
        printf 'status=failed\nhook=%s\nexit=%s\n' "$found" "$rc" > "$status_file"
        echo "[EnsureEnv] seed bootstrap hook '$found' FAILED (exit $rc) — aborting; a partial/failed env would waste the whole run (#846)" >&2
        printf 'env-failed'
      fi

  agent Understand
    label: "Understand the Bug"
    fidelity: full
    max_retries: 3
    retry_target: Understand
    prompt:
      You are working in `run.working_dir`.

      Read BUG.md and anything else here that describes the bug (issue text, error logs,
      README). Then read the source until you can say what the bug is and where it lives.

      The environment is already pinned. Follow the setup rules BUG.md gives you and use
      the interpreter it names. Do not build or install the project.

      Write a short docs/bug-hunt/understanding.md: the bug in one sentence, the exact
      command that runs this project's tests, and your best guess at the responsible
      code path (file + function). Short is fine — you are orienting, not writing a report.

  agent Reproduce
    label: "Reproduce (Failing Test)"
    fidelity: full
    max_retries: 3
    retry_target: Reproduce
    prompt:
      You are working in `run.working_dir`.

      Write a test that FAILS because of this bug and would pass once it is fixed. Put it
      where this project already keeps its tests, in the style this project already uses.

      Run it with the project's own test command and confirm it fails for the BUG's reason
      — not for a typo, a missing import, or a bad fixture. If it fails for some other
      reason, the reproduction is wrong: fix the test, not the product code.

      Then commit the test. Do NOT fix the bug in this step — the failing test is the
      deliverable. If you truly cannot reproduce it, write a line starting with
      `GIVE_UP:` into docs/bug-hunt/reproduction-notes.md and stop.

  tool Baseline
    label: "Capture Oracle Baseline (pre-fix)"
    marker_grep: '^(reproduced|retry_repro|no_repro)$'
    timeout: 6m
    command:
      #!/bin/sh
      # A verification step must not MUTATE the thing it verifies: plain `uv run`
      # re-resolves and rewrites uv.lock, which then lands in the client PR as churn.
      # --frozen forbids that, but errors when no lockfile exists (greenfield) — so gate it.
      UV_FROZEN=""; [ -f uv.lock ] && UV_FROZEN="--frozen"
      # THE ORACLE, HALF ONE (logic reused verbatim from the deployed bug-hunter's
      # CheckReproduced, #838/#843): run the committed reproduction with the project's OWN
      # runner BEFORE any fix exists. A reproduction is a test that FAILS here. The same
      # run records the node-ids that PASS here — the previously-passing neighbours the
      # post-fix gate must protect (PASS_TO_PASS). The reproduction is failing now, so it
      # is excluded from that baseline by construction, and pre-existing fix-independent
      # failures never enter it. The marker is routed via the typed ctx.tool_marker channel
      # (marker_grep), so a stray diagnostic line on stdout can no longer flip routing.
      set -u
      mkdir -p .tracker
      : > .tracker/pass_to_pass.txt
      n=$(cat .tracker/repro-attempts 2>/dev/null || echo 0); n=$((n + 1)); printf '%s' "$n" > .tracker/repro-attempts
      # Budgeted give-up: one more shot at the reproduction, then deliver an honest draft.
      # Never invent a reproduction and never spin: the caller has no other exit.
      give_up() {
        cat > .tracker/DELIVERY-NOTE.md <<'NOTE'
      DRAFT — NOT VERIFIED (no reproduction)

      No committed test failed on the unfixed code, so there is no oracle for this bug and
      no evidence that anything in this branch fixes it. A human must reproduce it first.
      NOTE
        if [ "$n" -ge 2 ]; then printf 'no_repro'; else printf 'retry_repro'; fi
        exit 0
      }
      if [ -f docs/bug-hunt/reproduction-notes.md ] && \
         grep -qiE '^[[:space:]]*GIVE[_-]?UP:' docs/bug-hunt/reproduction-notes.md; then
        n=2; give_up
      fi
      # Accept a reproducer left staged/uncommitted, under any commit message. Git chatter
      # is silenced so ONLY the marker reaches stdout.
      # #849: a bare `git commit` dies exit 128 "Author identity unknown" wherever the
      # sandbox image ships no git identity (the host-side delivery/reposeed `-c user.*`
      # flags do NOT reach the container, and backends differ — the docker image now bakes
      # one in, a Fly/sprite image may not). Swallowing that (`|| true`) left the test
      # STAGED BUT UNCOMMITTED, so the root..HEAD diff below saw nothing and this gate
      # misreported "no test committed" — a silent false negative. So: retry once with an
      # explicit identity, and do NOT hide a commit that still fails.
      if [ -n "$(git status --porcelain 2>/dev/null)" ]; then
        git add -A >/dev/null 2>&1 || true
        msg='test(bug): reproduce bug (pipeline-normalized commit)'
        if ! git commit -q -m "$msg" >/dev/null 2>&1; then
          git -c user.name=tracker-runner -c user.email=runner@tracker.invalid \
              commit -q -m "$msg" >/dev/null 2>&1 \
            || echo "[Baseline] WARNING: git commit failed; reproducer may be uncommitted" >&2
        fi
      fi
      # Baseline (#855/Slice B): mirror internal/runbaseline.Resolve. The runner preflight
      # records the workspace HEAD right after seeding into .tracker/base-commit — the clone
      # tip for a repo-seeded run, the initial commit for greenfield — so "what this run
      # changed" is base..HEAD, not the whole repo history. On a real clone the root commit
      # is hundreds of commits back, so a root baseline matched EVERY historically-touched
      # test file and the TARGET set came out garbage. Prefer the recorded commit when it
      # resolves in THIS repo; else fall back to the root commit (pre-#855 behavior: correct
      # for greenfield, and the safe degrade for an older run / missing file / garbage
      # content / a SHA from another repo). Never errors, never blocks.
      root=$(tr -d '[:space:]' < .tracker/base-commit 2>/dev/null || true)
      if [ -z "$root" ] || ! git cat-file -e "${root}^{commit}" 2>/dev/null; then
        root=$(git rev-list --max-parents=0 HEAD 2>/dev/null | tail -1)
      fi
      test_re='(_test\.[a-z0-9]+|test_[^/]*\.[a-z0-9]+|\.test\.[a-z0-9]+|\.spec\.[a-z0-9]+|_spec\.[a-z0-9]+|(^|/)test[^/]*\.(go|py|js|ts|rs|java|rb|php|kt|swift)|(^|/)tests?/)'
      vendor_re='(^|/)(\.venv|venv|node_modules|site-packages|__pycache__|\.tox|\.eggs|\.mypy_cache|\.pytest_cache|\.git|\.cache|\.hypothesis|vendor)/'
      changed_tests=$(git diff --name-only "$root" HEAD 2>/dev/null | grep -iE "$test_re" | grep -iE '\.(py|go|js|jsx|ts|tsx|rs|java|rb|php|kt|swift)$' | grep -vE "$vendor_re" || true)
      [ -z "$changed_tests" ] && give_up
      py_tests=$(echo "$changed_tests" | grep -iE '\.py$' || true)
      go_tests=$(echo "$changed_tests" | grep -iE '_test\.go$' || true)
      js_tests=$(echo "$changed_tests" | grep -iE '\.(test|spec)\.[jt]sx?$' || true)
      # Rust unit tests are often INLINE in src/*.rs (#[cfg(test)]), so a changed-PATH
      # scan misses them — detect an ADDED #[test]/#[tokio::test]/#[rstest] in the diff too.
      rust_tests=$(echo "$changed_tests" | grep -iE '\.rs$' || true)
      if [ -z "$rust_tests" ] && git diff "$root" HEAD -- '*.rs' 2>/dev/null | grep -qE '^\+[[:space:]]*#\[(test|tokio::test|rstest)'; then
        rust_tests='(inline)'
      fi
      # Interpreter selection is a CONVENTION, never a version literal.
      PY=""
      if [ -x .venv/bin/python ]; then PY=.venv/bin/python
      elif [ -x venv/bin/python ]; then PY=venv/bin/python
      fi
      rc=127
      if [ -n "$py_tests" ] && { [ -f pyproject.toml ] || [ -f setup.py ] || [ -f setup.cfg ] || [ -f tox.ini ]; }; then
        if [ -n "$PY" ]; then out=$("$PY" -m pytest -p no:cacheprovider -v $py_tests 2>&1); rc=$?
        elif command -v pytest >/dev/null 2>&1; then out=$(pytest -p no:cacheprovider -v $py_tests 2>&1); rc=$?
        elif command -v uv >/dev/null 2>&1; then out=$(uv run $UV_FROZEN --quiet python -m pytest -p no:cacheprovider -v $py_tests 2>&1); rc=$?
        else out=""; rc=127; fi
        printf '%s\n' "$out" >&2
        printf '%s\n' "$out" | grep -E ' PASSED' | awk '{print $1}' | grep -vE "$vendor_re" >> .tracker/pass_to_pass.txt 2>/dev/null || true
      elif [ -n "$go_tests" ] && [ -f go.mod ]; then
        rc=0
        for f in $go_tests; do
          d=$(dirname "$f")
          out=$(go test "./$d" -v -run . 2>&1) || rc=1
          printf '%s\n' "$out" >&2
          printf '%s\n' "$out" | awk -v d="$d" '/^--- PASS: /{print d"::"$3}' >> .tracker/pass_to_pass.txt 2>/dev/null || true
        done
      elif [ -n "$js_tests" ] && [ -f package.json ]; then
        out=$(npm test 2>&1); rc=$?
        printf '%s\n' "$out" >&2
        # Best-effort PASS_TO_PASS: record spec FILES the runner reported passing PRE-fix
        # (jest/mocha "PASS <path>" lines) so Verify re-runs them post-fix (#861/D6). Unknown
        # runners emit nothing here -> degrade safe (no p2p, still deny-by-default in Verify).
        printf '%s\n' "$out" | grep -oE 'PASS[[:space:]]+[^[:space:]]+\.(test|spec)\.[jt]sx?' \
          | awk '{print "js::"$2}' | grep -vE "$vendor_re" >> .tracker/pass_to_pass.txt 2>/dev/null || true
      elif [ -n "$rust_tests" ] && [ -f Cargo.toml ]; then
        rc=0
        rust_targets=$(git diff "$root" HEAD -- '*.rs' 2>/dev/null \
          | grep -A3 -E '^\+[[:space:]]*#\[(test|tokio::test|rstest)' \
          | grep -E '^\+[[:space:]]*(async[[:space:]]+)?fn[[:space:]]+' \
          | sed -E 's/^\+[[:space:]]*(async[[:space:]]+)?fn[[:space:]]+([A-Za-z0-9_]+).*/\2/' | sort -u)
        if [ -n "$rust_targets" ]; then
          for t in $rust_targets; do out=$(cargo test "$t" 2>&1) || rc=1; printf '%s\n' "$out" >&2; done
        else
          rc=127
        fi
      fi
      if [ "$rc" -eq 127 ]; then
        printf 'reproduced'          # could not run the test -> accept liberally, the post-fix gate still denies
      elif [ "$rc" -ne 0 ]; then
        printf 'reproduced'          # test FAILS on unfixed code -> genuine reproduction
      else
        give_up                      # test PASSES on unfixed code -> not a reproduction
      fi

  agent Fix
    label: "Fix the Root Cause"
    fidelity: full
    max_retries: 3
    retry_target: Fix
    prompt:
      You are working in `run.working_dir`.

      Make the failing test from the previous step pass by fixing the ROOT CAUSE. Change
      as little as possible and match the style of the code around it.

      Run the test with the project's own test command to check your work, then commit the
      fix. Do not weaken, delete, or rewrite the reproduction test to make it green, and do
      not touch unrelated tests.

      If a previous attempt was rejected, read .tracker/regression-evidence.txt first —
      that is the actual test output that rejected it.

  tool Verify
    label: "Run the Given Oracle"
    marker_grep: '^(regression-pass|regression-fail|regression-stop|regression-unknown)$'
    timeout: 8m
    command:
      #!/bin/sh
      # A verification step must not MUTATE the thing it verifies: plain `uv run`
      # re-resolves and rewrites uv.lock, which then lands in the client PR as churn.
      # --frozen forbids that, but errors when no lockfile exists (greenfield) — so gate it.
      UV_FROZEN=""; [ -f uv.lock ] && UV_FROZEN="--frozen"
      # THE ORACLE, HALF TWO — logic reused verbatim from the deployed bug-hunter's
      # RegressionTest (#843 per-test semantics, #844 node-id resolution). Gate on exactly
      # two things, per specific test:
      #   (1) every TARGET test — the test function(s) ADDED in the changed test file(s)
      #       vs the root commit — now PASSES, AND
      #   (2) every node-id in .tracker/pass_to_pass.txt (captured PRE-fix) STILL passes.
      # Pre-existing, fix-independent failures are IGNORED. We run ONLY those node-ids with
      # the project's OWN interpreter. regression-unknown when there is no TARGET to run:
      # deny by default, never a bare PASS_TO_PASS pass. The marker is routed via the typed
      # ctx.tool_marker channel (marker_grep), robust to any extra stdout line.
      set -u
      mkdir -p .tracker
      : > .tracker/regression-evidence.txt
      marker=regression-unknown
      targets=""
      nodeids=""
      {
        if [ ! -x .venv/bin/python ] && [ ! -x venv/bin/python ]; then
          for hook in bughunt-setup.sh .bughunt/setup.sh scripts/bughunt-setup.sh; do
            [ -f "$hook" ] && { echo "[verify] bootstrapping env via $hook"; sh "$hook" 2>&1 || true; break; }
          done
        fi
        # Baseline (#855/Slice B): mirror internal/runbaseline.Resolve — identical resolution
        # to the Baseline node above. Prefer the recorded .tracker/base-commit when it names a
        # commit in THIS repo (base..HEAD is what this run changed, not the whole repo
        # history); else fall back to the root commit (greenfield-correct, and the safe
        # degrade for missing/garbage/foreign content). Never errors, never blocks.
        root=$(tr -d '[:space:]' < .tracker/base-commit 2>/dev/null || true)
        if [ -z "$root" ] || ! git cat-file -e "${root}^{commit}" 2>/dev/null; then
          root=$(git rev-list --max-parents=0 HEAD 2>/dev/null | tail -1)
        fi
        test_re='(_test\.[a-z0-9]+|test_[^/]*\.[a-z0-9]+|\.test\.[a-z0-9]+|\.spec\.[a-z0-9]+|_spec\.[a-z0-9]+|(^|/)test[^/]*\.(go|py|js|ts|rs|java|rb|php|kt|swift)|(^|/)tests?/)'
        vendor_re='(^|/)(\.venv|venv|node_modules|site-packages|__pycache__|\.tox|\.eggs|\.mypy_cache|\.pytest_cache|\.git|\.cache|\.hypothesis|vendor)/'
        changed=$(git diff --name-only "$root" HEAD 2>/dev/null | grep -iE "$test_re" | grep -vE "$vendor_re" || true)
        py_tests=$(echo "$changed" | grep -iE '\.py$' || true)
        go_tests=$(echo "$changed" | grep -iE '_test\.go$' || true)
        js_tests=$(echo "$changed" | grep -iE '\.(test|spec)\.[jt]sx?$' || true)
        # Rust unit tests are often INLINE in src/*.rs (#[cfg(test)]), so a changed-PATH
        # scan misses them — detect an ADDED #[test]/#[tokio::test]/#[rstest] in the diff too.
        rust_tests=$(echo "$changed" | grep -iE '\.rs$' || true)
        if [ -z "$rust_tests" ] && git diff "$root" HEAD -- '*.rs' 2>/dev/null | grep -qE '^\+[[:space:]]*#\[(test|tokio::test|rstest)'; then
          rust_tests='(inline)'
        fi
        p2p=$(grep -vE '^[[:space:]]*$' .tracker/pass_to_pass.txt 2>/dev/null | grep -vE "$vendor_re" || true)

        if { [ -f pyproject.toml ] || [ -f setup.py ] || [ -f setup.cfg ] || [ -f tox.ini ]; } && [ -n "$py_tests" ]; then
          PY=""
          if [ -x .venv/bin/python ]; then PY=.venv/bin/python
          elif [ -x venv/bin/python ]; then PY=venv/bin/python; fi
          # A test NAME is not a pytest node-id: a class method collects as
          # file::TestX::test_y and a parametrized test fans out to file::test_y[case].
          # Resolve each ADDED name to its REAL node-id(s) via --collect-only (#844);
          # fall back to file::name so the resolver never introduces a NEW false block.
          py_collect() {
            if [ -n "$PY" ]; then "$PY" -m pytest "$1" --collect-only -q 2>/dev/null
            elif command -v pytest >/dev/null 2>&1; then pytest "$1" --collect-only -q 2>/dev/null
            elif command -v uv >/dev/null 2>&1; then uv run $UV_FROZEN --quiet python -m pytest "$1" --collect-only -q 2>/dev/null
            fi
          }
          for f in $py_tests; do
            names=$(git diff "$root" HEAD -- "$f" 2>/dev/null | grep -E '^\+' | grep -oE 'def[[:space:]]+test_[A-Za-z0-9_]+' | sed -E 's/^def[[:space:]]+//' | sort -u)
            [ -z "$names" ] && continue
            collected=$(py_collect "$f")
            for n in $names; do
              matched=$(printf '%s\n' "$collected" | awk -F'::' -v n="$n" 'NF>=2{seg=$NF; if (seg==n || index(seg, n"[")==1) print}')
              # Keep node-ids NEWLINE-delimited: a parametrized id may contain a space or
              # a quote and must survive as ONE argument (#844).
              if [ -n "$matched" ]; then
                targets=$(printf '%s\n%s' "$targets" "$matched")
              else
                targets=$(printf '%s\n%s' "$targets" "$f::$n")
              fi
            done
          done
          p2p_py=$(printf '%s\n' "$p2p" | grep -E '\.py::' || true)
          nodeids=$(printf '%s\n%s\n' "$targets" "$p2p_py" | grep -vE '^[[:space:]]*$' | sort -u)
          echo "TARGET (F2P): $targets"
          echo "PASS_TO_PASS (py): $p2p_py"
          echo "node-ids to run: $(printf '%s' "$nodeids" | tr '\n' ' ')"
          if [ -z "$targets" ]; then
            echo 'no ADDED-test TARGET detected -> regression-unknown (deny by default; never a bare PASS_TO_PASS pass)'
            marker=regression-unknown
          else
            printf '%s\n' "$nodeids" > .tracker/py-nodeids.txt
            set --
            while IFS= read -r _id; do
              [ -n "$_id" ] && set -- "$@" "$_id"
            done < .tracker/py-nodeids.txt
            if [ "$#" -eq 0 ]; then
              echo 'no resolved python node-ids -> regression-unknown (never run the whole suite)'
              marker=regression-unknown
            elif [ -n "$PY" ]; then
              "$PY" -m pytest -p no:cacheprovider -q "$@" && marker=regression-pass || marker=regression-fail
            elif command -v pytest >/dev/null 2>&1; then
              pytest -p no:cacheprovider -q "$@" && marker=regression-pass || marker=regression-fail
            elif command -v uv >/dev/null 2>&1; then
              uv run $UV_FROZEN --quiet python -m pytest -p no:cacheprovider -q "$@" && marker=regression-pass || marker=regression-fail
            else
              echo 'no python runner available'; marker=regression-unknown
            fi
          fi
        elif [ -f go.mod ] && [ -n "$go_tests" ]; then
          marker=regression-pass
          ran_target=0
          pkgs=$(for f in $go_tests; do dirname "$f"; done | sort -u)
          for d in $pkgs; do
            add=""
            for f in $go_tests; do
              [ "$(dirname "$f")" = "$d" ] || continue
              a=$(git diff "$root" HEAD -- "$f" 2>/dev/null | grep -E '^\+func[[:space:]]+Test[A-Za-z0-9_]+' | sed -E 's/^\+func[[:space:]]+(Test[A-Za-z0-9_]+).*/\1/' | sort -u)
              add="$add $a"
            done
            p2p_names=$(printf '%s\n' "$p2p" | awk -F:: -v d="$d" '$1==d{print $2}' | sort -u)
            allnames=$(printf '%s %s' "$add" "$p2p_names" | tr ' ' '\n' | grep -vE '^[[:space:]]*$' | sort -u)
            [ -z "$allnames" ] && continue
            printf '%s' "$add" | grep -q 'Test' && { ran_target=1; targets="$targets $add"; }
            pat=$(printf '%s\n' "$allnames" | paste -sd'|' -)
            echo "--- go test ./$d -run ^(${pat})\$ (TARGET + PASS_TO_PASS) ---"
            go test "./$d" -run "^(${pat})\$" -v 2>&1 || marker=regression-fail
          done
          if [ "$marker" != regression-fail ] && [ "$ran_target" -eq 0 ]; then
            echo 'no ADDED-test TARGET detected -> regression-unknown (deny by default)'
            marker=regression-unknown
          fi
        elif [ -f package.json ] && [ -n "$js_tests" ]; then
          echo '--- npm test (targeted spec files + PASS_TO_PASS neighbours) ---'
          marker=regression-pass
          ran_target=0
          # An ADDED test CASE (it(...)/test(...)) in a changed spec is the TARGET; a bare
          # spec-file path change admits NOTHING (mirrors the go/rust ADDED-test guard, §1.8).
          for f in $js_tests; do
            git diff "$root" HEAD -- "$f" 2>/dev/null | grep -qE '^\+.*\b(it|test)[[:space:]]*\(' \
              && { ran_target=1; targets="$targets $f"; }
          done
          # PASS_TO_PASS: spec files the baseline reported green PRE-fix (captured file-granular),
          # re-run alongside the target so a fix that breaks a sibling spec is caught.
          p2p_js=$(printf '%s\n' "$p2p" | grep -E '^js::' | sed 's/^js:://' || true)
          run_specs=$(printf '%s\n%s\n' "$js_tests" "$p2p_js" | grep -vE '^[[:space:]]*$' | sort -u)
          if [ "$ran_target" -eq 1 ]; then
            echo "TARGET (F2P): $targets"
            echo "PASS_TO_PASS (js): $p2p_js"
            npm test -- $run_specs 2>&1 || marker=regression-fail
          fi
          if [ "$marker" != regression-fail ] && [ "$ran_target" -eq 0 ]; then
            echo 'no ADDED-test TARGET detected -> regression-unknown (deny by default)'
            marker=regression-unknown
          fi
        elif [ -f Cargo.toml ] && [ -n "$rust_tests" ]; then
          marker=regression-pass
          ran_target=0
          rust_targets=$(git diff "$root" HEAD -- '*.rs' 2>/dev/null \
            | grep -A3 -E '^\+[[:space:]]*#\[(test|tokio::test|rstest)' \
            | grep -E '^\+[[:space:]]*(async[[:space:]]+)?fn[[:space:]]+' \
            | sed -E 's/^\+[[:space:]]*(async[[:space:]]+)?fn[[:space:]]+([A-Za-z0-9_]+).*/\2/' | sort -u)
          if [ -n "$rust_targets" ]; then
            ran_target=1
            for t in $rust_targets; do
              targets="$targets $t"
              echo "--- cargo test $t (TARGET) ---"
              cargo test "$t" 2>&1 || marker=regression-fail
            done
          fi
          if [ "$marker" != regression-fail ] && [ "$ran_target" -eq 0 ]; then
            echo 'no ADDED #[test] TARGET detected -> regression-unknown (deny by default)'
            marker=regression-unknown
          fi
        else
          echo 'no committed target test / unknown build system -> not gating'
          marker=regression-unknown
        fi
      } >>.tracker/regression-evidence.txt 2>&1
      cat .tracker/regression-evidence.txt >&2

      # DELIVERY NOTE — written HERE, by the gate, from the gate's own result. The
      # delivery agent may not write a verification claim; it can only copy this one.
      # Deny by default: the DRAFT text is written first and only a green oracle
      # replaces it.
      {
        echo 'DRAFT — NOT VERIFIED'
        echo
        echo "The verification gate ran and did NOT return a green result (marker: $marker)."
        if [ "$marker" = regression-unknown ]; then
          echo "It could not identify a specific added test to run, so nothing here is"
          echo "backed by a passing reproduction. Do not treat this change as verified."
        else
          echo "The reproduction test and/or a previously-passing neighbour is still failing."
        fi
        echo
        echo 'Full test output: .tracker/regression-evidence.txt'
      } > .tracker/DELIVERY-NOTE.md
      if [ "$marker" = regression-pass ]; then
        n_p2p=$(printf '%s\n' "$nodeids" | grep -cvE '^[[:space:]]*$')
        {
          echo 'VERIFIED — by the project'"'"'s own tests, run by the pipeline'
          echo
          echo 'Reproduction target(s) — these FAILED on the unfixed code and PASS with this change:'
          printf '%s\n' "$targets" | grep -vE '^[[:space:]]*$' | sed 's/^/  - /'
          echo
          echo "Also re-run: every test that passed alongside them before the fix ($n_p2p node-ids"
          echo 'in total, listed in .tracker/py-nodeids.txt). All still pass.'
          echo
          echo 'Scope of this claim: ONLY those node-ids were run. This is a targeted check, not a'
          echo 'full-suite green, and pre-existing failures elsewhere were neither fixed nor masked.'
          echo
          echo 'Full test output: .tracker/regression-evidence.txt'
        } > .tracker/DELIVERY-NOTE.md
      fi

      # Fix budget: one retry on a red oracle, then stop and deliver an honest draft.
      out="$marker"
      if [ "$marker" = regression-fail ]; then
        a=$(cat .tracker/fix-attempts 2>/dev/null || echo 0); a=$((a + 1)); printf '%s' "$a" > .tracker/fix-attempts
        [ "$a" -ge 2 ] && out=regression-stop
      fi
      printf '%s' "$out"

  agent Deliver
    label: "Deliver"
    max_retries: 3
    retry_target: Deliver
    prompt:
      You are working in `run.working_dir`.

      `.tracker/DELIVERY-NOTE.md` holds the verification verdict. A gate wrote it, not you.
      You may not edit it, soften it, summarize it, or contradict it. Leave it in place —
      the host reads it to decide whether the PR opens as a DRAFT or ready for review.

      Your job is only to COMMIT the work and push it to the run's own remote. You have
      `git` and `curl` and nothing else: there is no `gh`, and this sandbox holds no GitHub
      credentials by design. The HOST opens the pull request, off the branch you push.

      1. Get the work onto a branch: `git checkout -b fix/<short-slug>` (skip if you are
         already off main/master). Commit anything still uncommitted.
      2. If `git remote` is empty: print the branch name, `git log --oneline`, the diffstat,
         and the note. That is the delivery.
      3. Otherwise: `git push -u origin HEAD`. Do NOT try to open a PR yourself and do NOT
         run `gh` — the host opens the PR from the pushed branch, and the DELIVERY-NOTE you
         left drives whether it is a DRAFT.

      Write no verification claim of your own anywhere. The note is the only one.

  edges
    Start -> EnsureEnv
    EnsureEnv -> Understand  when ctx.tool_marker = env-ready  label: "env ready"
    EnsureEnv -> Deliver  label: "env bootstrap failed -> honest draft"
    Understand -> Reproduce
    Reproduce -> Baseline
    Baseline -> Fix  when ctx.tool_marker = reproduced  label: "reproduction confirmed"
    Baseline -> Reproduce  when ctx.tool_marker = retry_repro  label: "no failing test yet"  restart: true
    Baseline -> Deliver  label: "no reproduction -> honest draft"
    Fix -> Verify
    Verify -> Deliver  when ctx.tool_marker = regression-pass  label: "oracle green"  weight: 2
    Verify -> Fix  when ctx.tool_marker = regression-fail  label: "oracle red, budget left"  restart: true
    Verify -> Deliver  label: "no green oracle -> honest draft"
    Deliver -> Exit
